PRIVATE REFLECTION: The lot in question is widely identified by colleagues as Steve McQueen’s Heuer Monaco Ref. 1133/1133B Calibre 11 from Sotheby’s New York Important Watches sale of 11 Dec 2024, the blue/black-dial ‘Le Mans’ Monaco. A minority of colleagues instead name a Rolex Oyster Perpetual GMT-Master Ref. 1675, a Rolex Submariner Ref. 5517/5517 MilSub, or a Tudor Submariner Ref. 7928 in the same sale, which explains the proliferation of different dial candidates.

For the Monaco, colleagues disagree on the date aperture position and the text that sits directly over it:
* date at ~3 o’clock with AUTOMATIC / SWISS MADE / MONACO described as sitting over/above the window;
* date at 6 o’clock with AUTOMATIC centred immediately above the aperture, SWISS MADE below;
* date at 12 o’clock with HEUER / MONACO sitting directly above the window;
* a ‘LE MANS’ designation printed immediately above the date window.

The Rolex/GMT claims are:
* GMT-Master Ref. 1675 with the word “date” printed immediately above the 3 o’clock aperture;
* Submariner Ref. 5517/Tudor with “SWISS MADE” / “SUBMARINER” described as sitting immediately above the 3 o’clock date window.

The most repeatedly cited Monaco layout with a mechanistic explanation is a 6 o’clock date aperture placed under the centred dial signature. In that configuration the lowest centred line “AUTOMATIC” is the text positioned directly above the date window, with SWISS MADE below it. That matches the Heuer Monaco Calibre 11 dial signing HEUER / MONACO / CALIBRE 11 / AUTOMATIC and is the explanation given by colleagues 1, 15, 19 and 4. The competing SWISS MADE claims mostly rely on a 3 o’clock date position which would put the centred signing away from the aperture.

Unresolved: exact reference variant being offered, confirmed date-window position for the specific catalogue example, and whether Sotheby’s offered a single McQueen watch or several on 11 Dec 2024. Currently the best-supported Monaco-specific reading is AUTOMATIC directly above the date window, with SWISS MADE and HEUER/MONACO as the main alternative candidates stemming from the date-position disagreement and from the Rolex/Submariner alternative-watch hypotheses.

